// Committed signing base (no secret). project.yml's `configFiles` points here.
//
// The Apple Developer Team ID must NOT live in this public repo, so it's kept
// in a gitignored local override that this file optionally pulls in. The `?`
// makes the include tolerant of a missing file:
//   - CI / fresh clones have no local override → no Team ID → xcodegen +
//     simulator builds still work (CI signs nothing).
//   - Locally, App/DODApp.local.xcconfig supplies DEVELOPMENT_TEAM so device
//     builds and Archives sign without the "requires a development team" error.
//
// Create the override after a fresh clone with your Team ID (the OU field of
// your signing cert — `security find-certificate … | openssl x509 -noout -subject`):
//   echo 'DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = XXXXXXXXXX' > App/DODApp.local.xcconfig
//
// DUT-23: app-identity key for anonymous comment POSTs, surfaced to the app as
// the DODCommentAPIKey Info.plist value and sent as the X-DOD-App-Key header.
// BLANK here on purpose so NO secret lives in this public repo; CI injects the
// real value at archive time from the DOD_COMMENT_API_KEY GitHub secret (see
// .github/workflows/release.yml). To exercise comment posting from a LOCAL
// build, set a real value in the gitignored DODApp.local.xcconfig override.
DOD_COMMENT_API_KEY =
// DUT-680: GA4 Measurement Protocol creds, surfaced to the app as the
// GA4MeasurementID / GA4APISecret Info.plist values. The GA4Transport mirrors
// in-app recipe/article OPENS into Google Analytics 4 as content traffic.
// BLANK here on purpose so NO secret lives in this public repo — with either
// value blank the transport no-ops (dev / PR / unconfigured builds send
// nothing). CI injects the real values at archive time from the
// GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID / GA4_API_SECRET GitHub secrets (mirror the
// DOD_COMMENT_API_KEY pattern in .github/workflows/release.yml). To exercise
// GA4 from a LOCAL build, set real values in the gitignored
// DODApp.local.xcconfig override.
GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID =
GA4_API_SECRET =
#include? "DODApp.local.xcconfig"
